From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] input: rsinput: quiesce the MCU across system sleep

The MCU streams input reports continuously and is told nothing at
suspend. Reports arriving while the GENI UART is suspending cause its
IRQ handler to return IRQ_NONE repeatedly, after which spurious-IRQ
detection disables the UART IRQ and the controller stays dead until
reboot.

Quiesce the MCU before the port suspends by dropping its enable and
reset lines, mirroring rsinput_remove(). rsinput_resume() already
performs the full power-on through rsinput_init_commands().

Originally-by: Luke Johnson <jaewun@me.com>
Ported from Armada: https://github.com/armada-os/armada/blob/410bcf26a67f3e5d38e487d0ec84c5632f2bc3f6/packages/kernel/patches/1005-input-rsinput-quiesce-the-mcu-across-system-sleep.patch
---
--- a/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
@@ -626,6 +626,24 @@
     regulator_disable(drv->vdd);
 }

+static int rsinput_suspend(struct device *dev)
+{
+    struct rsinput_driver *drv = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+    /*
+     * Stop continuous MCU reports before the UART suspends; otherwise the
+     * UART IRQ can be disabled as spurious. rsinput_resume() powers the
+     * MCU back on through rsinput_init_commands().
+     */
+    if (drv->enable_gpio)
+        gpiod_set_value_cansleep(drv->enable_gpio, 0);
+
+    if (drv->reset_gpio)
+        gpiod_set_value_cansleep(drv->reset_gpio, 0);
+
+    return 0;
+}
+
 static int rsinput_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
     struct rsinput_driver *drv = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
@@ -633,7 +651,7 @@
     return rsinput_init_commands(drv);
 }

-static DEFINE_SIMPLE_DEV_PM_OPS(rsinput_pm_ops, NULL, rsinput_resume);
+static DEFINE_SIMPLE_DEV_PM_OPS(rsinput_pm_ops, rsinput_suspend, rsinput_resume);

 static const struct of_device_id rsinput_of_match[] = {
     { .compatible = "gamepad,rsinput" },
